# Logistics Team Member
  text: New York, New York, United States
# About CookUnity:
  text: Food has lost its soul to modern convenience. And with it, it has lost the power to nourish, inspire, and connect us. So in 2018, CookUnity 
  text: empower Chefs to nourish the world.
  text: If that mission has you hungry in more ways than one, you’ve found the right job posting.
  text: The Logistics team member is responsible for helping drive a smooth, on-time handover from FFM to last mile each morning. This role starts t
  text: Daily Metrics Review & Pickup Planning
  text: Start each shift by reviewing the previous day's logistics metrics, including FFM-to-last-mile handover timeliness and overall delivery dela
  text: Review the supervisor count from the final hour of FFM operations to assess FFM capacity and anticipate its impact on last-mile handover.
  text: When FFM is behind schedule, adjust and push driver pickup times to account for the delay.
  text: When FFM is on track, review yesterday's delivery performance and fine-tune today's driver pickup times to help meet the delivery window.
  text: Logistics Service & Order Checks
  text: Check the Logistics Service to confirm all orders have been assigned.
  text: Review for any orders with integration errors and resolve or escalate as needed.
  text: Handover & Dispatch Execution
  text: Complete the daily audit checklist to confirm handover readiness across all routes.
  text: Confirm all routes are ready for handover and have been picked up.
  text: Oversee cart-to-truck and pallet-to-truck loading.
  text: Track middle-mile truck arrivals to ensure on-time dispatch.
  text: Help ensure the end-to-end handover process runs smoothly and on time from FFM to last mile.
  text: Driver & Route Issue Resolution
  text: Troubleshoot driver issues in real time, including scanning problems, missing or damaged bags, and replacing damaged product.
  text: Identify and resolve route coverage gaps as they come up.
  text: Define pickup schedules for 3PL partners based on route distance and mileage.
  text: Coordinate with 3PL's on pickup times and driver changes.
  text: Manage 3PL no-shows by ensuring the affected route is covered or picked up by the 3PL.
  text: 1+ years of experience in logistics, warehouse, distribution, or a related operations role.
  text: Bilingual (English/Spanish) preferred.
  text: Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to make real-time decisions under time pressure.
  text: Comfortable coordinating directly with third-party logistics (3PL) providers and drivers.
  text: Familiarity with reviewing logistics/delivery metrics and dashboards.
  text: Ability to work an early morning shift, including weekends/holidays as needed based on operational demand.
  text: Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, particularly around checklist-driven audits.
  text: Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull up to 50 lbs regularly.
  text: Ability to stand, walk, and bend for extended periods throughout the shift.
  text: Ability to work in varying temperature environments, including cold storage/refrigerated areas.
  text: Ability to move quickly and safely between the loading dock, warehouse floor, and office areas.
  text: 🩺 Health Insurance coverage with Cigna
  text: 🚀 Opportunity for advancement
# Compensation
  text: Pay Range for this position
  text: CookUnity is an Equal Opportunity Employer
  text: A quick note for all candidates
